@@ -46,6 +46,20 @@ Which port to listen on. Applies to both TCP and Unix sockets.
 
 Default: 6432
 
+### proxy_protocol
+
+Accept an optional PROXY protocol v1 header before the PostgreSQL startup
+packet. When enabled, the source address from a TCP4 or TCP6 header is included
+in connection log prefixes. Connections without a PROXY header, including
+direct connections and SSL negotiation, continue to work normally.
+
+The reported address is used only for logging; it does not replace the peer
+address used for authentication or access control. Only enable this setting
+when incoming connections are restricted to trusted proxies, since clients can
+otherwise supply arbitrary source addresses in their headers.
+
+Default: 0 (disabled)
+
